# Media Workbench v2 — screen comp R3: Results + Grade v2 drawer (DARKROOM — the only Darkroom comp in the set)
schema: "0.4"
id: mw-screen-results-grade-v2
type: image
service: gemini
model: gemini-3.1-flash-image
quality: high
prompt:
  text: |
    A straight-on screenshot of a macOS 14 app window in a near-black "darkroom" treatment for judging generated images. Canvas #0A0A0B, panels #141415, primary text #E8E6E3, secondary text #8A8785, a single warm brass accent #C9A227 used only for the selection ring. Green #4ADE80 and red #F87171 appear only as pass/fail gates. SF Pro type, SF Mono for numbers. Traffic lights top left; no sidebar on this screen.

    Top: a slim one-line context bar on #141415: "pricing-hero · gemini/gemini-3.1-flash-image · attempt 3/4 · 1m42s · $0.06".

    Centre-left: the hero artifact, a vivid generated illustration (abstract layered glass panels in deep teal and coral on dark, a website pricing hero), fit inside the field with dark margin, not cropped. It is the brightest, most colourful thing on screen.

    Bottom: a left-aligned candidate rail of four thumbnails, each with a small circular score badge pinned to the bottom-right corner of the thumbnail, never covering the centre of the image: "84" green badge with a 2pt brass ring (selected), "78" green badge, "61" red badge, and a fourth placeholder tile with a thin progress bar "62%", its badge equally pinned to the bottom-right corner.

    Right: a 320pt drawer on #141415 over the field, titled "Grade", with a small chip "alibaba · decision-model-preview".
    - Header: "84 / 100" large, and a small green "PASSED".
    - Four criterion rows, each: name, weight × score, a provenance chip, and below it exactly ten small square cells in a row; NOT a gradient; most cells near-black; probability shown by brightness, not by position along a ramp; a thin light tick marks the expected score:
      "composition 0.35 × 88" chip "prompt" — a single very bright cell at position 9 (or 8), neighbours dim — confident;
      "palette 0.30 × 86" chip "house:palette" — a single very bright cell at position 9 (or 8), neighbours dim — confident;
      "legibility 0.20 × 79" chip "house:type", small "required" — a single very bright cell at position 9 (or 8), neighbours dim — confident;
      "brand-voice 0.15 × 74" chip "project:voice" — two separate bright cells at positions 3 and 8 with dark cells between — uncertain, with a tiny diamond marker.
    - A divider, then two small rows: "reject_if  embedded text  P 0.04" and "watermark  P 0.02".
    - At the bottom two small buttons: "Override…" and "Revise".

    Artifact dominant, chrome recedes, numbers crisp. Short legible labels and numbers only.
  negative: >
    garbled text, lorem ipsum, watermark, mobile frame, browser chrome, Windows UI,
    perspective tilt, synthesizer/audio-hardware look, CAD tool, manuscript editor,
    blue or teal UI accent, neon glow, glassmorphism chrome, light mode, sidebar, pie chart, gauge dial,
    gradient bar, progress bar ramp, gauge, badge centred over image
  style: "UI design screen comp, straight-on screenshot framing, no perspective, no camera tilt, crisp pixel-sharp interface, Lightroom-like restraint"
output:
  formats:
    - format: png
      quality: 95
  dimensions:
    width: 2560
    height: 1600
    aspect_ratio: "16:10"
eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  criteria:
    depicts_the_product:
      weight: 0.4
      description: "reads as a media-generation request/review/grading tool, specifically judging generated image candidates with per-criterion scores from an automated judge"
    follows_spec:
      weight: 0.35
      description: "shows (1) a dominant generated artifact plus a left-aligned scored candidate rail with gate-coloured badges and a brass selection ring; (2) a right Grade drawer with a weighted total and per-criterion 10-cell distribution strips with an expected-score tick, at least one visibly split; (3) provenance chips such as house:palette and project:voice; (4) the one-line context bar naming run, provider/model, attempt and cost"
    macos_native:
      weight: 0.25
      description: "reads as a native macOS 14 window (traffic lights, SF type) in a dark custom treatment, not a web dashboard"
  reject_if:
    - depicts a different product category (photo-editing suite without scores, CAD tool, manuscript editor, audio hardware, web page)
    - primary labels (criterion names, scores, 84 / 100) are unreadable or garbled
tags: [screen-comp, macos, media-workbench, v2]
